{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>הוכה</b> — The meaning is like <b>יומם השמש לא יככה</b> (by day the sun does not smite you). It was the taunt of the foe: just as the sun smites the grass and it dries, so his heart failed, for the generation of natural [vitality] departed from the heart, by which the soul is joined to the flesh, and he cannot eat bread, for he is sated without food. And the meaning is doubled, for food brings in [new] parts to replace what the enemy [i.e., the destroying force] removes — and this is known from the wisdom of the constellations."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is textually difficult in places; ליחת התולדת rendered hyper-literally as 'the generation of natural [vitality],' and שהוא יביא חלקים כנגד מה שיוליך האויד read as 'it brings in parts to replace what the enemy removes,' though the syntax is compressed and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:47.662715547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}